her.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2921140a76dcbd9cc0960c9fd28cc956f95adf0f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 22 at 3:24PM MDT until August 22 at 6:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\nSouthwestern Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nNorth Central Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 630 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 324 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area.\nBetween 1 and 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nIndian Creek, Willow Creek, Garber Creek, South Platte River,\nMiddle Garber Creek, Rainbow Creek, Pine Creek, West Bear Creek,\nDeer Creek, Plum Creek, Big Dry Creek, Bear Creek and North\nGarber Creek. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are\nexpected over the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nHighlands Ranch, Littleton, Roxborough Park, Louviers, Chatfield\nReservoir, Sprucewood, Kassler and Columbine.","ends":"2026-08-22T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.79babdd62d6ef165ae91cdad79407999210da5fc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.79babdd62d6ef165ae91cdad79407999210da5fc.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 22 at 2:13PM MDT until August 22 at 5:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"FFWBOU\n\nThe National Weather Service in Denver has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEast Central Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 500 PM MDT.\n\n* At 213 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Between\n1 and 2.5 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts\nup to 0.5 inches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, gulches,\nroads, and poor drainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nCastlewood Canyon.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nCherry Creek, Willow Creek, East Plum Creek and Lake Gulch.","ends":"2026-08-22T17:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.caa774c820a22455f92d2ad6d63655b8379725e7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.caa774c820a22455f92d2ad6d63655b8379725e7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-22T18:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 221850 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1250 PM MDT Sat Aug 22 2026 - Highest coverage of showers and storms expected today, along with a few severe storms and locally heavy rainfall this afternoon and evening. - Scattered afternoon and evening showers and storms through Thursday. A risk of a couple severe storms each day. - Temperatures se","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-22T19:27:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Sunday... Scattered to numerous showers and storms, most with wetting rains, will push east from the mountains across the plains late this afternoon and evening. Humidity values will be moderate today, and then expect very good recovery tonight in all areas. Sunday will feature scattered afternoon and evening